# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the tests that crash a parse on purpose
# (the [crash-guard] tests; tests/CMakeLists.txt applies this file to
# them alone through LSAN_OPTIONS).
#
# LLVM's CrashRecoveryContext recovers a crashed parse by jumping out of
# the signal handler back into runCrashGuarded: the frames of the crashed
# ClangTool::run (its CompilerInstance, ASTContext, FileManager, VFS
# overlays, the frontend action) are abandoned without running their
# destructors, and nothing references their heap allocations afterwards.
# That is the documented cost of in-process crash containment in LLVM,
# not a leak this repository can free. The TU-local indexes vycor itself
# abandons are retained explicitly (callgraph/RetainUntilExit.h) and need
# no entry here. Every other test, and any leak outside a guarded parse
# in these tests, is still reported.
leak:vycor::runCrashGuarded
